WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:02.800
- Welcome everyone to another
episode of Firm Learning.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.360
And today I wanna talk about
how to dress like a consultant.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.540
And of course we all know that consultants

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.630
like to wear suits, shirts,
sometimes also ties,

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:14.820
so, in today's video, I do
wanna go beyond the obvious

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.180
and also talk about the
more similar differences,

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.020
the less obvious things
that do made alone,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.900
really can make a difference,
when you choose your wardrobe

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:23.733
for consulting.

00:00:23.733 --> 00:00:25.620
This video focuses on the male wardrobe,

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.049
since the gentleman edition,

00:00:27.049 --> 00:00:28.900
I might also create a video about

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.700
female wardrobe in the future.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.533
Let me know in the comments

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:33.720
whether this would be a topic
you're interested in as well,

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.740
I might need some female
support on that though.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.070
The topic I want to connect this to

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.900
is maybe a little bit controversial,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.530
so, feel free to provide your opinion,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.230
your views also in the comments.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.240
But it is at least my humble observation,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.450
that in especially MBB firms,

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.691
so these leading strategy
consulting firms,

00:00:48.691 --> 00:00:51.410
McKinsey, BCG, Bain, and the like,

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.763
the quota of people with a
working class background.

00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:56.830
So, the quota of people

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:00.230
of first generation
academics is rather low.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:03.790
So, the question of course
is, why is this the case?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.960
Surely there are no hard
criteria in the interviews

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.410
discriminating against
these kinds of backgrounds.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.670
It seems clear to me though
that at least in academia,

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.950
these types of phenomena are way describe,

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.110
there is also very famous sociologists

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:19.571
called Pierre Bourdieu, who
coined the term "Habitus."

00:01:19.571 --> 00:01:22.591
So, describes how different
people have different habitus,

00:01:22.591 --> 00:01:26.500
which can be loosely
translated to social status.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.470
But Pierre Bourdieu is very explicit,

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.110
that this status is to be
defined far beyond only money.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.870
So, there's much more to it
than just your financial means.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:39.240
And the big part of it is
also your cultural capital.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.620
So, for instance, how to
address in certain situations

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.990
and maybe also how not to
dress in certain situations.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:46.930
And this is arguably a knowledge

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:49.070
that people with certain
backgrounds may be lack,

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.198
because of course, this is not
something that you will learn

00:01:51.198 --> 00:01:53.655
during your business
administration studies.

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:56.780
These are often things that
you really learn at home

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.154
maybe from your parents, from your peers.

00:01:59.154 --> 00:02:02.320
Of course, everyone knows
that you need to wear a suit

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.962
a shirt, maybe a tire
to your job interview,

00:02:04.962 --> 00:02:08.120
but people often lack the
understanding beyond that, right?

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.021
So, what type of suit
are you supposed to wear?

00:02:11.021 --> 00:02:13.800
What type of shirt are
you supposed to wear?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.104
So, these are exactly the things

00:02:15.104 --> 00:02:17.300
I want to help you with today,

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.180
these fine distinctions as
Pierre Bourdieu would call it,

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.840
that really can have a
very significant impact

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.370
on you personally and also professionally.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.810
So, let's start with the suits.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.740
So, what suits should you wear?

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.377
And just to provide a
little bit of context,

00:02:31.377 --> 00:02:34.650
I also want to talk about a
slightly more formal attire

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.630
and how this fits into the bigger picture

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.730
of what you should wear as a consultant.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.260
I think the first thing to understand

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.100
is that usually for men's wear,

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.940
you distinguish evening
attire and daytime attire.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.900
So, let's start with
formal evening attire.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.410
And there are usually
three types of suits,

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.350
dress suits that you wear as a man.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.760
The most formal one is a Tail coat.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.917
So, this is what often is described

00:02:57.917 --> 00:03:00.350
as a white tie dress code,

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:03.329
a tail coat, sometimes
worn for gala dinners,

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:06.430
frankly rather rarely really used today,

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.160
but that's the most formal attire

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.900
that you can wear as a man.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.010
The second most formal, and
this maybe something that

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:15.160
some of you have also more
experienced with, is a Tuxedo.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.310
So, a tuxedo are things that
you will also wear often,

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.367
this is worn again in more
usual regular gala events,

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:23.870
often also in the evening
of a wedding for instance.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.976
A tuxedo would be something like this.

00:03:26.976 --> 00:03:28.950
Now, we can make just a video about that,

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.610
now, I don't want to go
too much into the details

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.230
of how a tuxedos may be different
from a more regular suit.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.980
But surely I hope it's
clear, that you will not wear

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:41.140
neither a Tail coat nor
tuxedo as a consultant.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.930
And the number three for the
more formal evening attires,

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.560
is a Black suit.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.330
So, if a tuxedo is maybe
a little bit too much

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.410
and you are on a very
formal event in the evening,

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.490
you might want to wear a Black suit.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.010
So, that's the evening attire

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:57.030
and now let's talk about
the daytime attire.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:01.150
And daytime usually means
until about 6:00 PM.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.833
So, that's the logic that you will hear.

00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:07.350
And the most formal daytime
attire is a Cutaway.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.580
So probably, also contrast
to a take called cutaways

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.800
also cuts, as many
people like to call them

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.650
are still rather common,
You often see them

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.976
at more formal weddings
during the daytime.

00:04:16.976 --> 00:04:18.540
So that's number one, the cut,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.070
the number two most formal
is called the Stresemann,

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.360
also called a Black lounge suit.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.010
I will likely insert a
picture somewhere here,

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.470
because, frankly also don't have one.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:29.360
And then number three
is a Black suit as well.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.500
So where do I want to get it?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.720
Because indeed, all these things are not

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.430
what you will wear
usually as a consultant.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.470
And the error that some people are doing

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:39.250
is that they are wearing a black suit

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.270
to the regular consulting job.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.043
This is a typical error, because again,

00:04:43.043 --> 00:04:48.043
black suits are usually formal
attire, for formal events,

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.100
not for your day to day business,

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.040
not for your day to day clothing.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.430
So, what type of suit
would you wear instead?

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:57.870
Well these are darker suits
that are not black though.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.900
The typical colors would be an anthracite,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.870
so dark anthracite color.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.890
Another typical color would
be just a dark gray tone

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.470
for instance, something like
this that you could wear

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.600
or also a dark blue.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.359
Personally, I really like dark blue,

00:05:12.359 --> 00:05:13.989
just in general as a
color and also for suits,

00:05:13.989 --> 00:05:16.960
I think this often fits really well.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.530
Next, let's talk about shirts,

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:20.240
because, for sure there are many errors

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.680
that you can make with shirts.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.324
And the first thing
that maybe comes to mind

00:05:23.324 --> 00:05:26.730
is a plain wide shirt.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:29.110
So can you wear a plain white shirt?

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:31.330
and here I'd say, hmm, yes,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.060
but maybe it's not the best shirt.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.070
I mean, first of all,
truth is also MBB firms,

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.306
so maybe especially MBB firms,

00:05:36.306 --> 00:05:39.160
many people wear white shirts.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.670
So, this is for sure not uncommon,

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.872
you will see many people wearing them.

00:05:42.872 --> 00:05:44.610
But now, linking this back to this point

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:49.480
on more formal attire,
traditionally plain white shirts

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.170
are shirts that are
worn for formal attire.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:55.630
And indeed, so what shirt
do you wear instead?

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.810
So, let me just show a couple of examples.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:59.552
So usually, what's
recommended maybe rather

00:05:59.552 --> 00:06:04.379
instead of a plain white,
is a simple light blue.

00:06:04.379 --> 00:06:06.580
So, be careful here with a tone of blue,

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.080
the tone really matters and
principle, you want to go

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.540
with a very light blue like this,

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.380
so this would be a good alternative.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.731
Another nice touch is a light stripe.

00:06:16.731 --> 00:06:20.010
Something like this, so
blue and white stripes,

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:23.000
this also makes a very
nice day to day shirt,

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.441
that you can very well wear
also during business times,

00:06:25.441 --> 00:06:27.800
where for instance, you
should be a bit careful

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:28.980
just to provide an example.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.354
It is a shirt like this.

00:06:31.354 --> 00:06:35.890
This is also blue and probably
still border line okay.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:39.500
But notice how this blue
already is a little bit darker

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.333
than this other blue.

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:42.010
Now, I'm not sure whether you
can see it well in the video

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.580
but, this blue is a little bit darker

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:46.440
and this darky makes it a
little bit more sportive.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.550
And again, we don't
want to go with too much

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.330
of sportive shirts in these occasions,

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.640
but now let's talk about
patterns of shirts.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.260
And I do think that you
can also wear patterns,

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.320
which are maybe a little more extravagant

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:59.800
than just simple stripes,

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.710
so let's look at an example like this,

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.530
again, not sure where you
can see it in the video,

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:06.313
but, this is a very
light, light blue pattern.

00:07:06.313 --> 00:07:07.598
That is a bit more complex though,

00:07:07.598 --> 00:07:10.820
with more cross type of things in here.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.010
Why this is very light,

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:13.950
I'd say this is still okay.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:17.080
Here the point is, how
visible these patterns are.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.780
And again, let's contrast
that for instance,

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:22.211
with a shirt like this

00:07:22.211 --> 00:07:25.570
with more very, very bold stripes pattern.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:28.330
This is too much, this is too sportive.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:31.280
This is not a type of
shirt that you should wear.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.850
Let's talk about something else,

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.680
and this is now the collar.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.565
And here also one very typical error,

00:07:36.565 --> 00:07:39.280
and now here I'm deliberately
choosing this shirt

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.930
which is already sportive,

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:44.430
is this type of collar with
two buttons in the collar.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:48.120
This type of color is
called a button down collar.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:51.520
So, if you wear this, the
first very big four power

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:53.490
is if you wear such a shirt

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.810
without closing down your
buttons of the collar.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.240
So, this just an absolute no good,

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.140
this is, has only to do with consulting,

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.070
but also just in your leisure and so on,

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.336
button down shirts are
always supposed to be worn

00:08:04.336 --> 00:08:06.789
with closed buttons here at the collar.

00:08:06.789 --> 00:08:08.520
But I would even go one step beyond

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.490
and to say that, this
type of collar in general,

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:15.150
is considered to be a
very sportive collar type.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:16.670
So, I would claim that in general

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:18.900
shirts with a button down collar,

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.760
should not be worn in more, you know,

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.330
formal consulting day
to day business attire.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:26.340
Let's now talk about shirts
with colored buttons.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.230
So here again, you see a very
sportive version of a shirt.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.236
See how more sportive versions

00:08:30.236 --> 00:08:32.570
more often come also with button down,

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:33.880
again, you just fits it,

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.000
because, it's also sportive collar type.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.370
But indeed, here with this example

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.900
you have these dark black buttons.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.850
One thing that I think
is just, don't do it.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.027
You see quite frequently our shirts

00:08:45.027 --> 00:08:46.930
that maybe even white, right?

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.070
So white shirts, which makes
them already very formal

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.480
and then they come with,
for instance black buttons

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:54.234
or somehow colored buttons.

00:08:54.234 --> 00:08:56.020
And I guess maybe some people believe

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:58.140
that this is like a
great stylistic choice,

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.870
here again, just don't do it.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:03.200
So now, let's next talk about
the cuffs of your shirt.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.830
And probably the two most
common variations are

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.190
so-called Barrel cuffs,

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.990
So more sportive of ones
and also Double cuffs.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.140
So I need to look at the screen

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:12.529
to know all these English terms.

00:09:12.529 --> 00:09:15.240
But here the simple double cuff

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.740
would be something like this.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.308
So cuff that then you fold

00:09:19.308 --> 00:09:22.548
and then put together and
then connect via cufflinks.

00:09:22.548 --> 00:09:26.040
So, this is usually the
more formal type of cuffs.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.210
And the other type that is considered

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.900
the more sportive one, is the single cuff

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.940
or barrel cuff is what
it's called in English.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.670
And that's the cuff where
just with simple buttons,

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.770
without folding them,
you can connect them.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:40.690
Today it's very common to
just wear these simpler cuffs,

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:41.980
also for your shirt,

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.220
So, this is absolutely fine,

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.140
this is absolutely what you can wear.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.096
To be aware if you want
to be a bit more formal,

00:09:47.096 --> 00:09:48.831
a bit more dressy,

00:09:48.831 --> 00:09:51.540
these types of cuffs, the
double cuffs work as well,

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.010
and then of course you
have the opportunity

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:54.460
to combine this with some cufflinks.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:58.260
But just a nice way of
having some jewelry, maybe,

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.168
even as a man on your cuffs,

00:10:00.168 --> 00:10:02.430
now, I don't want to go here
too much into the detail,

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:05.030
surely, don't overdo it
with your cufflinks, right?

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.841
I mean, you can be extremely extravagant.

00:10:06.841 --> 00:10:09.690
I mean, you'll also choose
maybe some more simple,

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:12.280
more decent motives,
but I trust in general

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:14.530
that's an important
distinction to know as well.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.150
Let's now discuss ties.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:19.320
And here probably the reality
and also for MBB consulting

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.980
is that ties are not that
commonly worn anymore.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.090
And you often will
adjust a little bit more

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.750
to the client office or
what the clients is doing,

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:28.660
if they're wearing ties,

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:30.400
then you will likely wear a ties as well.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.520
Probably, the majority
of the clients I work for

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.240
that we didn't need to wear a tie,

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.513
but, even if you don't need to wear a tie,

00:10:35.513 --> 00:10:37.930
I think it's always the
best practice to have a tie

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:38.920
in your bag.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.280
If maybe on short notice, you
need to join another location,

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.480
maybe join a workshop,
a meeting, whatever,

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:45.950
maybe even at another client,

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.860
that you are ready to wear a
tie whenever this is required.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.620
So if you do wear a tie
similar with the other things,

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.730
I would choose more plain,
more regular colors,

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.840
so here, for instance,
dark green, dark blue,

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:00.750
some very light more decent
motives, surely, are okay,

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.790
is maybe here, you see
this very light green

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:05.195
and blue motive that you
see here on this tie,

00:11:05.195 --> 00:11:07.530
but this is what I would go for.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:08.688
Surely, I would be a bit careful

00:11:08.688 --> 00:11:12.140
when your motives are more
colorful, more playful,

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.720
maybe like something like this.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:15.326
This would be a more sportive tie.

00:11:15.326 --> 00:11:18.319
This probably is not the
best fit for consulting.

00:11:18.319 --> 00:11:21.390
So, let's now talk about
the shoes, because surely,

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.947
this is also an important
part of your outfit.

00:11:23.947 --> 00:11:26.700
And here, frankly, I would in general

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.830
just go with dark black shoes.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.050
This is where you usually
will not go wrong.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:35.210
So very classical, typical
shoe type like this.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.160
I believe these are called Oxfords.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.837
Now probably, the real experts
in the comments will tell me

00:11:38.837 --> 00:11:41.030
that this is not right or
maybe called differently.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.520
Let me know, I'll be interested.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.170
But this is just a very
typical, nice form,

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:46.460
and maybe a little bit more sportive,

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.800
are these brogue, since
I believe they're called

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:51.630
also similar with a bit
more appliances here

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.600
at the top part of the shoe.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.450
So, this for sure is absolutely fine,

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:56.510
you can wear this.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:59.370
We won't be a bit careful of brown shoes.

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.640
But this to some extent
can be okay as well.

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.170
It often looks very sportive

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.840
and it require a little bit
more of stylistic command,

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.810
to really combine them in the right way.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.680
If you do wanna be a bit more extravagant,

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.289
surely, there's also some other models,

00:12:11.289 --> 00:12:13.540
like some nice monks for instance,

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.830
they can work quite well.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.380
I will try to include a
couple of pictures here

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.590
for these types of shoes,

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.560
but if in doubt, go for very
nice, clean, simple Oxfords

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:21.890
and you will do nothing wrong.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.210
Let's next talk about belts,

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.090
because usually, you will use belts

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.501
to hold your suit into position.

00:12:26.501 --> 00:12:28.050
Some suits don't require one,

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.685
but I'd say most of them
that you will buy do,

00:12:29.685 --> 00:12:32.466
until there's one very
basic and simple rule,

00:12:32.466 --> 00:12:35.288
this is that the belt should have both

00:12:35.288 --> 00:12:39.250
the color and the material of the shoes

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.083
that you are wearing.

00:12:40.083 --> 00:12:40.916
The color and the material of
the shoes that you're wearing.

00:12:43.827 --> 00:12:45.370
So, if you just follow my recommendation

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:48.012
and go with very plain
and black leather shoes,

00:12:48.012 --> 00:12:51.760
then just pick a plain black leather belt

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:52.820
and you will be fine.

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:54.270
If you do choose brown shoes,

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:56.620
then of course also choose a brown belt.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.350
If you go for buckskin material,

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:01.280
make sure that your belt is
from buckskin leather as well.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.050
Again, color and material of your shoes

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.459
and your belt should match.

00:13:05.459 --> 00:13:08.630
This is the very basic, simple
rule that you should follow.

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:10.650
So, last one no list,
let's talk about accessory.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.780
So, what are the additional
things that you can wear?

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:14.590
We all ready talked about cufflinks.

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:17.600
Another big question that I
often get are pocket squares.

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.710
So, should you wear pocket squares or not,

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:21.130
the idea of pocket squares is

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:23.830
that this is something that
you might be able to put here

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.760
into the pocket of your suit.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:26.878
So you see this sometimes,

00:13:26.878 --> 00:13:29.060
my general recommendation here would be,

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.470
to not do it in consulting.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:31.500
I think it's very unusual,

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.460
only very, very few people will do it.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.200
My general recommendation for these

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.814
more business type of situations,

00:13:36.814 --> 00:13:39.110
would be to not wear pocket squares,

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.250
to not use pocket squares like this.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.330
And last but at least,
another point are the watches.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.020
So, think a watch of
course is always something

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:49.097
that nicely compliments a
man's, a gentleman's outfit.

00:13:49.097 --> 00:13:51.280
So of course, you need to be a bit careful

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.310
with what type of watch you are wearing.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.160
So, what's very popular

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.220
and I think no problem
all are smart watches.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:57.990
So, for instance you own an apple watch

00:13:57.990 --> 00:13:59.250
that truly no problem at all

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.237
and can also be quite
handy for checking emails,

00:14:01.237 --> 00:14:03.060
checking your calendar and so on.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:05.240
If you want to wear more
traditional mechanical watch,

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.046
that's of course, absolutely okay as well,

00:14:07.046 --> 00:14:09.180
just two recommendations
that I would give you

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:11.750
from my humble experience is first,

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.590
I probably would avoid watches

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:16.970
that cost more than 10,000 Euro or $10,000

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.700
or very expensive watches.

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.280
Again, in general, you want to
avoid creating the impression

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:22.830
in front of your clients

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.620
that you are extremely
rich, extremely loaded.

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:28.150
And then also second, certain brands.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.390
Even though maybe they
are below 10,000 Euro,

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.323
just to provide a very general threshold,

00:14:32.323 --> 00:14:34.470
they are a bit controversial

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.850
and they are associated
with certain thoughts

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.683
that some people have.

00:14:38.683 --> 00:14:41.160
So, I think you're the
classic one, our Rolex watches

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.160
I think in general,
Rolex watches are great,

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.722
I can understand why
many people like them.

00:14:44.722 --> 00:14:47.770
But maybe if you have one,
rather keep it to yourself

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.730
for your leisure time,
maybe with your friends,

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:51.360
if you hang out in the evening,

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.100
but maybe not during your work day,

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:54.760
if you work in consulting.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.557
Again this might just create
the wrong impression for you.

00:14:57.557 --> 00:14:59.620
And I hope you can see my
point from the beginning

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.550
that to say it with Pierre Bourdieu,

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:04.267
the differences can often be quite subtle,

00:15:04.267 --> 00:15:05.910
but I would be interested in your opinion.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:07.910
I mean, do you agree, I'm
in no means wanna claim

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.710
that I am the biggest fashion master,

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.790
happy to also learn more
about these things from you.

